  Line 223: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 01',title:'The question in the dark',villain:'riddler',scene:'THE NARROWS',caption:'A QUESTION WITH NO ANSWER',text:`<p>A green question mark is painted on the shutter of a closed pawnshop. Bruce photographs it from across the street. It is not a confession—just the first hint that someone wants the city to know he is watching.</p><p>Alfred finds a string of riddles in old police reports. Bruce files them away, unsure whether the author is a criminal, a prankster, or both.</p>`},

  Line 224: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 02',title:'A smile on the wire',villain:'joker',scene:'GOTHAM BROADCAST',caption:'LAUGHTER AFTER MIDNIGHT',text:`<p>Every screen in a downtown electronics shop flickers to life at once. A pale face smiles through the static, telling a joke no one in the room finds funny. The broadcast ends with a burst of confetti and a list of abandoned buildings.</p><p>Bruce watches the recording twice. The danger is not the punchline. It is how carefully the speaker studied his audience.</p>`},

  Line 225: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 03',title:'The coin that never lands',villain:'twoface',scene:'OLD COURTHOUSE',caption:'JUSTICE ON BOTH SIDES',text:`<p>Harvey Dent once believed a fair trial could change Gotham. Now a scarred former prosecutor lets a coin decide which version of justice will speak for him. One side is bright; the other is dark and worn.</p><p>Bruce keeps Harvey’s old campaign button beside the case notes. He will not reduce his friend to the damage done to him.</p>`},

  Line 226: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 04',title:'Something beneath the river',villain:'croc',scene:'EAST END DRAINS',caption:'EYES BELOW THE WATER',text:`<p>Workers refuse to enter a storm tunnel after hearing heavy footsteps beneath the grates. A hulking figure is seen only in the ripples and the brief flash of yellow eyes.</p><p>The newspapers call him a monster. Bruce writes a different question in the margin: what happened to the boy before the city gave him that name?</p>`},

  Line 227: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 05',title:'The tea-party invitation',villain:'hatter',scene:'ABANDONED THEATER',caption:'ONE SEAT LEFT EMPTY',text:`<p>In a derelict playhouse, a tiny paper invitation waits on a velvet chair. It promises a perfect world to anyone willing to follow the White Rabbit. The ink is fresh; the theater has been empty for years.</p><p>Bruce recognizes the language of a trap dressed as comfort. Some people do not want power over a city. They want power over one person at a time.</p>`},

  Line 228: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 06',title:'The cold front',villain:'freeze',scene:'GOTHAM HARBOR',caption:'WINTER IN THE WRONG SEASON',text:`<p>A shipment of medical equipment disappears from a waterfront laboratory. Frost feathers the inside of a locked storage door, though the night outside is warm.</p><p>The lead points to Victor Fries, a scientist trying to keep his wife alive. Bruce marks the name carefully. A desperate motive does not make dangerous methods harmless.</p>`},

  Line 229: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 07',title:'The man who broke a wall',villain:'bane',scene:'BLACKGATE PRISON',caption:'STRENGTH IS A STRATEGY',text:`<p>A transfer report describes a prisoner who studies every guard rotation and every weakness in the building. Bane does not waste strength; he saves it for the moment it matters.</p><p>Bruce adds endurance drills to his training. Winning a fight, he realizes, may begin long before the first blow.</p>`},

  Line 230: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 08',title:'The clown’s calling card',villain:'joker',scene:'MONTOYA CIRCUS',caption:'THE SHOW WILL GO ON',text:`<p>A shuttered circus tent is found ringed with playing cards. Somewhere inside, a music box turns by itself. The officers who enter hear applause from an empty grandstand.</p><p>Bruce studies the scene photographs. The performer wants fear, but he also wants an audience. That need may be the most dangerous clue of all.</p>`},

  Line 231: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 09',title:'A city-sized puzzle',villain:'riddler',scene:'FINANCIAL DISTRICT',caption:'FOLLOW THE GREEN LIGHT',text:`<p>Traffic signals across three blocks change in a sequence that spells out a riddle. The pattern leads to a locked service room—and a second riddle hidden inside it.</p><p>Bruce maps the route without entering the buildings. Whoever designed the game is testing patience as much as intelligence.</p>`},

  Line 232: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 10',title:'Harvey’s other face',villain:'twoface',scene:'GOTHAM CENTRAL',caption:'A COIN IN THE EVIDENCE ROOM',text:`<p>A witness refuses to testify after receiving a silver coin with a scorched edge. Harvey’s old colleagues want to protect him from the investigation; Harvey would have demanded the truth.</p><p>Bruce asks Alfred to keep the original case files safe. Memory can preserve a person’s best self, even when the present tries to erase it.</p>`},

  Line 233: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 11',title:'The king below',villain:'croc',scene:'OLD SEWER LINE',caption:'THE TUNNELS HAVE A KING',text:`<p>A missing-persons report leads to a forgotten passage beneath the river. The marks on the concrete are too high for an ordinary man, and the torn steel bars bend outward.</p><p>Bruce brings a rescue map to the police instead of charging underground alone. Preparation is not cowardice; it is how you make sure someone comes back.</p>`},

  Line 234: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 12',title:'A dream with locked doors',villain:'hatter',scene:'WONDERLAND ROOM',caption:'WAKE UP, GOTHAM',text:`<p>Several people describe the same impossible tea party, down to the ticking clock and the empty chair. Their accounts point toward a doctor who has learned to make fantasy feel safer than waking life.</p><p>Bruce begins reading about coercion and trauma. The mind is not a puzzle box to force open. A victim needs a way out, not another person holding the key.</p>`},

  Line 235: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 13',title:'A promise in the ice',villain:'freeze',scene:'CRYOGENICS LAB',caption:'LOVE FROZEN IN TIME',text:`<p>Victor Fries leaves a message asking for a single component to stabilize Nora’s chamber. It is the first time his trail sounds less like a threat and more like a plea.</p><p>Bruce asks Wayne Medical to review the research. There may be a way to help without letting a desperate man endanger anyone else.</p>`},

  Line 236: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 14',title:'Bane’s careful silence',villain:'bane',scene:'PORT ADAMS',caption:'THE STRONGEST MAN WAITS',text:`<p>A crate of experimental medical supplies vanishes from the port. The theft is clean, with no broken locks and no witnesses willing to talk. Bane has made the city look in the wrong direction.</p><p>Bruce studies the timing. A patient opponent can turn a city’s routines into a weapon.</p>`},

  Line 237: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 15',title:'The punchline is a warning',villain:'joker',scene:'PARK ROW',caption:'NO ONE IS LAUGHING',text:`<p>At a charity hall, the lights go out for eleven seconds. When they return, every guest has a paper smile on the table and the donation ledger is gone. No one is hurt, but the message is unmistakable.</p><p>Bruce asks the staff what they saw before asking what they lost. Fear makes people forget that their safety matters more than a ledger.</p>`},

  Line 238: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 16',title:'Riddles on the rooftops',villain:'riddler',scene:'ROOFTOP GRID',caption:'THE NEXT CLUE IS ABOVE YOU',text:`<p>Green markers appear on rooftops overlooking the financial district. Each one points to a place where Gotham failed someone: a shuttered clinic, an empty school, a neglected shelter.</p><p>Bruce sees the cruelty inside the cleverness. The Riddler may know the city’s wounds, but he treats them as props in a game.</p>`},

  Line 239: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 17',title:'The courthouse divided',villain:'twoface',scene:'GOTHAM COURTHOUSE',caption:'ONE VERDICT, TWO OUTCOMES',text:`<p>Harvey sends a sealed envelope to Bruce. Inside is a list of people he wants protected from his own gang. The handwriting shifts from careful to jagged halfway down the page.</p><p>Bruce does not mistake the letter for an apology. He sees it as a chance to keep innocent people out of the crossfire.</p>`},

  Line 240: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 18',title:'The river remembers',villain:'croc',scene:'FLOODED UNDERPASS',caption:'A RESCUE IN THE DARK',text:`<p>Rising water traps a maintenance crew in a tunnel. Something moves beneath the surface, then lifts a steel gate from its hinges. The workers emerge shaken but alive.</p><p>Bruce cannot tell whether Croc saved them or simply cleared his path. Either way, the next search will need a boat, a plan, and a team.</p>`},

  Line 241: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 19',title:'The clockwork rabbit',villain:'hatter',scene:'CLOCKTOWER',caption:'TIME IS RUNNING OUT',text:`<p>A clocktower chimes thirteen times. A trail of brass gears leads to a locked room where a frightened witness has been hidden in plain sight.</p><p>Alfred reminds Bruce that rescuing someone means listening to them after the danger passes. The exit is only the beginning of feeling safe again.</p>`},

  Line 242: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 20',title:'Whiteout at the docks',villain:'freeze',scene:'GOTHAM DOCKS',caption:'THE HARBOR TURNS TO GLASS',text:`<p>A wave of freezing mist crawls across the docks as Victor tries to retrieve a power cell. Workers are stranded behind the ice, too afraid to cross the slick metal walkways.</p><p>Bruce coordinates a safe evacuation with the harbor crew. He will face Fries if he must, but the people in danger come first.</p>`},

  Line 243: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 21',title:'A test of endurance',villain:'bane',scene:'NARROWS ROOFLINE',caption:'NO SHORTCUT THROUGH FEAR',text:`<p>Bane leaves a trail of staged emergencies across the Narrows. Each one forces responders to split their attention. The trap is not a single fight; it is exhaustion.</p><p>Bruce changes the plan: call in help, rotate teams, and refuse to let pride set the pace. The city is stronger when no one has to carry it alone.</p>`},

  Line 244: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 22',title:'The joker takes the stage',villain:'joker',scene:'MONTOYA PLAYHOUSE',caption:'THE HOUSE LIGHTS GO OUT',text:`<p>The old playhouse is filled with laughing recordings and painted spotlights. The Joker wants the entire city to watch his performance, but the people inside are not an audience—they are hostages.</p><p>Bruce studies the exits first. A dramatic entrance can wait until everyone has a way out.</p>`},

  Line 245: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 23',title:'The answer beneath the question',villain:'riddler',scene:'WAYNE STATION',caption:'EVERY CLUE LEAVES A TRACE',text:`<p>A final riddle points to a substation carrying power to a hospital. Bruce spots the hidden override before the lights go out and alerts the engineers.</p><p>The puzzle is solved, but the lesson is larger: cleverness without care can become another kind of cruelty.</p>`},

  Line 246: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 24',title:'A chance for Harvey',villain:'twoface',scene:'ACE CHEMICALS',caption:'THE COIN FALLS',text:`<p>Harvey’s crew corners a bookkeeper who once helped build his career. The coin spins across a catwalk and lands on the scarred side. Bruce steps between them before the verdict can become irreversible.</p><p>He speaks to Harvey by name, not by nickname. One honest voice cannot undo everything, but it can leave a door open.</p>`},

  Line 247: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 25',title:'A truce in the tunnels',villain:'croc',scene:'UNDERCITY',caption:'THE WAY OUT IS TOGETHER',text:`<p>Bruce finds Croc guarding a group of unhoused people from a collapsing tunnel. Neither trusts the other, but the roof is coming down and there is no time for an argument.</p><p>They guide everyone to the surface. Croc disappears before the police arrive, leaving Bruce with more questions than answers—and one less reason to call him a monster.</p>`},

  Line 248: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 26',title:'The last tea party',villain:'hatter',scene:'WINTER GARDEN',caption:'THE CLOCK STOPS HERE',text:`<p>The Mad Hatter’s elaborate set is built around a greenhouse clock. The people he drew into his fantasy are scared, confused, and ready to choose their own way home.</p><p>Bruce keeps his voice calm and the room bright. The spell ends not with a punch, but with each guest remembering their own name.</p>`},

  Line 249: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 27',title:'A cure is not a cure',villain:'freeze',scene:'GOTHAM MEDICAL',caption:'HOPE NEEDS MORE THAN ICE',text:`<p>Victor’s power cell is recovered before the laboratory fails. The research is imperfect, but the doctors find a safer path to keep Nora stable while they continue their work.</p><p>Fries surrenders without a fight. Bruce sees a future case that may not need to be a battle at all.</p>`},

  Line 250: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 28',title:'The city wakes',villain:'bane',scene:'GOTHAM ROOFTOPS',caption:'DAWN OVER THE NARROWS',text:`<p>Bane’s final move is a coordinated strike meant to make Gotham believe resistance is pointless. Instead, neighbors open doors, medics share supplies, and officers protect the evacuation routes.</p><p>Bruce faces Bane after the last civilians are safe. Strength matters, but it is not the only strength in the city.</p>`},

