275: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 10',title:'Harvey’s other face',villain:'twoface',scene:'GOTHAM CENTRAL',caption:'A COIN IN THE EVIDENCE ROOM',text:`<p>A witness refuses to testify after receiving a silver coin with a scorched edge. Harvey’s old colleagues want to protect him from the investigation; Harvey would have demanded the truth.</p><p>Bruce asks Alfred to keep the original case files safe. Memory can preserve a person’s best self, even when the present tries to erase it.</p>`},
276: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 11',title:'The king below',villain:'croc',scene:'OLD SEWER LINE',caption:'THE TUNNELS HAVE A KING',text:`<p>A missing-persons report leads to a forgotten passage beneath the river. The marks on the concrete are too high for an ordinary man, and the torn steel bars bend outward.</p><p>Bruce brings a rescue map to the police instead of charging underground alone. Preparation is not cowardice; it is how you make sure someone comes back.</p>`},
277: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 12',title:'A dream with locked doors',villain:'hatter',scene:'WONDERLAND ROOM',caption:'WAKE UP, GOTHAM',text:`<p>Several people describe the same impossible tea party, down to the ticking clock and the empty chair. Their accounts point toward a doctor who has learned to make fantasy feel safer than waking life.</p><p>Bruce begins reading about coercion and trauma. The mind is not a puzzle box to force open. A victim needs a way out, not another person holding the key.</p>`},
278: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 13',title:'A promise in the ice',villain:'freeze',scene:'CRYOGENICS LAB',caption:'LOVE FROZEN IN TIME',text:`<p>Victor Fries leaves a message asking for a single component to stabilize Nora’s chamber. It is the first time his trail sounds less like a threat and more like a plea.</p><p>Bruce asks Wayne Medical to review the research. There may be a way to help without letting a desperate man endanger anyone else.</p>`},
279: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 14',title:'Bane’s careful silence',villain:'bane',scene:'PORT ADAMS',caption:'THE STRONGEST MAN WAITS',text:`<p>A crate of experimental medical supplies vanishes from the port. The theft is clean, with no broken locks and no witnesses willing to talk. Bane has made the city look in the wrong direction.</p><p>Bruce studies the timing. A patient opponent can turn a city’s routines into a weapon.</p>`},
280: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 15',title:'The punchline is a warning',villain:'joker',scene:'PARK ROW',caption:'NO ONE IS LAUGHING',text:`<p>At a charity hall, the lights go out for eleven seconds. When they return, every guest has a paper smile on the table and the donation ledger is gone. No one is hurt, but the message is unmistakable.</p><p>Bruce asks the staff what they saw before asking what they lost. Fear makes people forget that their safety matters more than a ledger.</p>`},
281: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 16',title:'Riddles on the rooftops',villain:'riddler',scene:'ROOFTOP GRID',caption:'THE NEXT CLUE IS ABOVE YOU',text:`<p>Green markers appear on rooftops overlooking the financial district. Each one points to a place where Gotham failed someone: a shuttered clinic, an empty school, a neglected shelter.</p><p>Bruce sees the cruelty inside the cleverness. The Riddler may know the city’s wounds, but he treats them as props in a game.</p>`},
282: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 17',title:'The courthouse divided',villain:'twoface',scene:'GOTHAM COURTHOUSE',caption:'ONE VERDICT, TWO OUTCOMES',text:`<p>Harvey sends a sealed envelope to Bruce. Inside is a list of people he wants protected from his own gang. The handwriting shifts from careful to jagged halfway down the page.</p><p>Bruce does not mistake the letter for an apology. He sees it as a chance to keep innocent people out of the crossfire.</p>`},
283: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 18',title:'The river remembers',villain:'croc',scene:'FLOODED UNDERPASS',caption:'A RESCUE IN THE DARK',text:`<p>Rising water traps a maintenance crew in a tunnel. Something moves beneath the surface, then lifts a steel gate from its hinges. The workers emerge shaken but alive.</p><p>Bruce cannot tell whether Croc saved them or simply cleared his path. Either way, the next search will need a boat, a plan, and a team.</p>`},
284: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 19',title:'The clockwork rabbit',villain:'hatter',scene:'CLOCKTOWER',caption:'TIME IS RUNNING OUT',text:`<p>A clocktower chimes thirteen times. A trail of brass gears leads to a locked room where a frightened witness has been hidden in plain sight.</p><p>Alfred reminds Bruce that rescuing someone means listening to them after the danger passes. The exit is only the beginning of feeling safe again.</p>`},
285: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 20',title:'Whiteout at the docks',villain:'freeze',scene:'GOTHAM DOCKS',caption:'THE HARBOR TURNS TO GLASS',text:`<p>A wave of freezing mist crawls across the docks as Victor tries to retrieve a power cell. Workers are stranded behind the ice, too afraid to cross the slick metal walkways.</p><p>Bruce coordinates a safe evacuation with the harbor crew. He will face Fries if he must, but the people in danger come first.</p>`},
286: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 21',title:'A test of endurance',villain:'bane',scene:'NARROWS ROOFLINE',caption:'NO SHORTCUT THROUGH FEAR',text:`<p>Bane leaves a trail of staged emergencies across the Narrows. Each one forces responders to split their attention. The trap is not a single fight; it is exhaustion.</p><p>Bruce changes the plan: call in help, rotate teams, and refuse to let pride set the pace. The city is stronger when no one has to carry it alone.</p>`},
287: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 22',title:'The joker takes the stage',villain:'joker',scene:'MONTOYA PLAYHOUSE',caption:'THE HOUSE LIGHTS GO OUT',text:`<p>The old playhouse is filled with laughing recordings and painted spotlights. The Joker wants the entire city to watch his performance, but the people inside are not an audience—they are hostages.</p><p>Bruce studies the exits first. A dramatic entrance can wait until everyone has a way out.</p>`},
288: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 23',title:'The answer beneath the question',villain:'riddler',scene:'WAYNE STATION',caption:'EVERY CLUE LEAVES A TRACE',text:`<p>A final riddle points to a substation carrying power to a hospital. Bruce spots the hidden override before the lights go out and alerts the engineers.</p><p>The puzzle is solved, but the lesson is larger: cleverness without care can become another kind of cruelty.</p>`},
289: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 24',title:'A chance for Harvey',villain:'twoface',scene:'ACE CHEMICALS',caption:'THE COIN FALLS',text:`<p>Harvey’s crew corners a bookkeeper who once helped build his career. The coin spins across a catwalk and lands on the scarred side. Bruce steps between them before the verdict can become irreversible.</p><p>He speaks to Harvey by name, not by nickname. One honest voice cannot undo everything, but it can leave a door open.</p>`},
290: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 25',title:'A truce in the tunnels',villain:'croc',scene:'UNDERCITY',caption:'THE WAY OUT IS TOGETHER',text:`<p>Bruce finds Croc guarding a group of unhoused people from a collapsing tunnel. Neither trusts the other, but the roof is coming down and there is no time for an argument.</p><p>They guide everyone to the surface. Croc disappears before the police arrive, leaving Bruce with more questions than answers—and one less reason to call him a monster.</p>`},
291: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 26',title:'The last tea party',villain:'hatter',scene:'WINTER GARDEN',caption:'THE CLOCK STOPS HERE',text:`<p>The Mad Hatter’s elaborate set is built around a greenhouse clock. The people he drew into his fantasy are scared, confused, and ready to choose their own way home.</p><p>Bruce keeps his voice calm and the room bright. The spell ends not with a punch, but with each guest remembering their own name.</p>`},
292: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 27',title:'A cure is not a cure',villain:'freeze',scene:'GOTHAM MEDICAL',caption:'HOPE NEEDS MORE THAN ICE',text:`<p>Victor’s power cell is recovered before the laboratory fails. The research is imperfect, but the doctors find a safer path to keep Nora stable while they continue their work.</p><p>Fries surrenders without a fight. Bruce sees a future case that may not need to be a battle at all.</p>`},
293: {date:'GOTHAM · CASE FILE 28',title:'The city wakes',villain:'bane',scene:'GOTHAM ROOFTOPS',caption:'DAWN OVER THE NARROWS',text:`<p>Bane’s final move is a coordinated strike meant to make Gotham believe resistance is pointless. Instead, neighbors open doors, medics share supplies, and officers protect the evacuation routes.</p><p>Bruce faces Bane after the last civilians are safe. Strength matters, but it is not the only strength in the city.</p>`},
294: {date:'GOTHAM · BEFORE DAWN',title:'A place to begin',scene:'WAYNE CAVE',caption:'ONE PROMISE. ONE FIRST STEP.',text:'<p>Alfred has left the gear ready: the field guide on the bench, prototypes on the armor table, the suit in its display frame, and the Batmobile resting beneath the stone ceiling. The elevator waits at the far end of the cave. Nothing here is finished, and nobody pretends otherwise.</p><p>Bruce takes in the quiet workshop and the steady lights. Beyond the cave lies a city full of strangers, each with a story he cannot know yet. He cannot undo the night that changed his life. He can choose what he does with the nights still ahead.</p><p class="quote">One man. One promise. A first step into the dark.</p><p>Explore the cave, inspect every piece of equipment, collect Riddler trophies, and take the elevator when you are ready.</p>'}
